WEBVTT

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:08.040
A station with people on board needs food, water, air and spare parts, all the time.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:18.200
People have lived aboard the International Space Station without a break since November 2000.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:23.050
Since 2012, private companies carry much of its cargo,

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:26.360
and some boosters now fly back and land.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:35.590
Even up there, a trace of air drags the station down, so it must be pushed back up.

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:41.120
To meet it, cargo ships start lower and faster, then catch up.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:50.110
The station weighs about 420 tonnes and circles Earth 16 times a day.

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:55.450
Now check your delivery. Cheaper launches mean more science per dollar.

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:03.170
<v Chicho>Reusing a rocket is like reusing a truck. Nobody throws away a truck after one trip.

